; An OUTER tag applied to a rule whose body is a NOMINAL SET (the tag-258 idiom / single-arm form).
; Since a named non-generic 258 set NOMINALIZES (Phase 2.2), the INNER 258 tag is OWNED by the
; nominal's own encoding struct and no longer flattens onto the holder — so the outer `#6.24` is the
; ONLY tag level in the reference-site encoding, and the `#6.24(<258-set>)` double-tag collision class
; is closed STRUCTURALLY by nominalization (there is nothing left to stack). This fixture pins that
; outcome; the depth-suffixed stacking of genuinely-flattened NON-set tags (`{name}_tag_encoding` at
; level 1, `{name}_tag{k}_encoding` at level k>=2) is pinned by
; `robustness_tests::stacked_tag_encoding_members_are_depth_disambiguated` (non-258 tags, which stay
; transparent aliases whose tag DOES flatten).
;
; - `homogeneous_inner` / `homogeneous` — outer mandatory tag 24 over a single-arm 258 set nominal:
;   `HomogeneousEncoding` carries only `inner_tag_encoding: Option<cbor_event::Sz>` (the 258 lives in
;   `HomogeneousInnerEncoding`), and `homogeneous` serializes as tag 24 then a nominal delegation.
; - `heterogeneous_set` / `heterogeneous` — outer mandatory tag 24 over the two-arm 258 set nominal:
;   again only the outer `Option<cbor_event::Sz>` sits on the holder; the optional-258
;   `TagPresenceEncoding` lives inside the nominal set.
; - `elem_tagged` / `outer_over_array` — a MANDATORY outer tag 24 over an ARRAY whose ELEMENT is a 258
;   set nominal: the element serializes via its own nominal deserialize, so no `{field}_elem_tag*`
;   member is minted on the holder at all — the element boundary owns its tag through the nominal.
; - `holder` — embeds all three in record-field position so member-side (de)serialize compiles + roundtrips.
homogeneous_inner = #6.258([* uint])
homogeneous = #6.24(homogeneous_inner)
heterogeneous_set = #6.258([* uint]) / [* uint]
heterogeneous = #6.24(heterogeneous_set)
elem_tagged = #6.258([* uint])
outer_over_array = #6.24([* elem_tagged])
holder = [h: homogeneous, s: heterogeneous, a: outer_over_array]
